Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.04,0:00:12.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,everyone I'm happy to have Dylan here.\N大家好，我很高兴 Dylan 能来。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.72,0:00:18.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first time I saw one of his videos was an interview when he talked about all the way up to\N我第一次看到他的视频，是在一次采访中，他谈到了方方面面
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.39,0:00:22.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,CPUs to talk about like neoclouds and why they have the right to exist and that was super interesting for me\NCPU 讨论像新云厂商这类话题，以及它们为何有存在的正当理由，这对我来说非常有趣。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.97,0:00:28.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,because the theme of today is all like what are the new infrastructure primitives now that agents are here and so you\N因为今天的主题是，如今智能体已经出现，新的基础设施基本单元是什么
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.66,0:00:34.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,are tricking at that really well at that point why neoclouds are different from hyperscalers and why they should exist.\N你当时就很好地抓住了重点：新云厂商与超大规模云厂商有何不同，以及它们为何应该存在。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.58,0:00:36.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,So can you share any of that with us?\N那你能跟我们分享一些吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.88,0:00:37.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sure.\N当然。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.48,0:00:41.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean um in the age of AI the hyperscalers were a little bit slow to move right Google\N我的意思是，在人工智能时代，超大规模云厂商的反应稍微有点迟缓，比如谷歌
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.68,0:00:49.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Amazon Microsoft bit slow to move into AI and so a whole new crop of companies popped up and there was\N亚马逊和微软在进入人工智能领域时反应较慢，因此涌现出一大批全新的公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.15,0:00:55.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,a new low bar right there's no need for a lot of the complex software that Amazon Microsoft Google had built\N出现了一个新的低门槛：不再需要亚马逊、微软、谷歌构建的那些复杂软件。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.39,0:01:00.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,up and a lot of this in fact slowed down AI right they had custom networks that were actually not that\N而且事实上，很多这类东西反而拖慢了 AI：他们的定制网络对 AI 并不算好，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.99,0:01:07.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,great for AI they were more focused around reliability and storage traffic rather than you know doing an AllReduce across\N这些网络更关注可靠性和存储流量，而不是做跨节点的 AllReduce。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.53,0:01:12.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,the network or something like this so so there was a lot of things that these large cloud companies these hyper\N网络之类的东西。所以这些大型云公司、这些超大规模云厂商拥有的很多东西，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.36,0:01:19.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,scalers had that neoclouds could just skip right and and then build focused optimized solutions and deliver much lower cost\N新云厂商可以直接跳过，转而构建专注优化的解决方案，把成本降得多得多。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.19,0:01:26.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,because they have much lower overhead right there's not 20,000 Google PMs sitting in a meeting at these neoclouds right\N因为它们的开销低得多，这些新云厂商里可没有两万名谷歌产品经理在开会。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.92,0:01:34.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,although some of them have started hiring Google PMs and slowed down the the the neoclouds they they they\N尽管其中一些公司已经开始招聘谷歌的产品经理，并放缓了新云厂商的扩张步伐。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.52,0:01:39.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,just moved fast on energy they moved fast on bringing up GPU clusters and so they were able to carve out\N他们迅速推进能源建设，快速搭建 GPU 集群，因此开辟出了一块市场。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.93,0:01:44.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,a market right and then you know those are the early ones and then since then there have been a lot\N一个市场，然后你知道，那些是早期的，从那以后就有很多了
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.49,0:01:51.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,more copycats or followers many who haven't succeeded many who are succeeding right it really is like a a battle of\N更多跟风者或追随者，有失败的，也有正在成功的，这真像一场较量。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.77,0:01:56.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,like who's the most competent And so are all the cuz there's like I think you said there's like an order\N谁是最能干的？所以大家都很厉害，我觉得你说过，好像有个顺序
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.04,0:02:03.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's like a 200 of these neoclouds or give or take right and so are there differentiations between them that\N这类新云厂商大概有两百个左右，或者差不多，它们之间有什么区别吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.03,0:02:09.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,you see like are are some of them just copying the the sort of software stack that these first ones did\N你看，有些公司是不是只是在复制最早那批公司的软件栈？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.91,0:02:15.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,or they doing something else like anything that you've seen that have been successful and less successful across these neoclouds?\N还是说他们在做别的事情？你看到这些新云厂商里，哪些成功、哪些不成功？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.59,0:02:20.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah so there's a variety of things that separate them right so we have something called ClusterMAX that\N是的，它们之间有很多不同之处，比如我们有名为 ClusterMAX 的产品。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.23,0:02:30.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,ranks all the neoclouds but we test for various things such as observability reliability networking security um orchestration all\N它会给所有新云厂商排名，但我们测试的是可观测性、可靠性、网络、安全和编排等各方面。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.77,0:02:36.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,these sorts of things are different right like does does someone test for their GPUs to be working properly\N这类事情是不一样的。比如，有人会测试 GPU 在用户不用时是否仍正常工作吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.83,0:02:42.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,in when the GPUs are idle for a user right that's active health check or a passive health check hey\N这就是主动健康检查或被动健康检查。风扇转速对吗？功耗对吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.58,0:02:46.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,are the fans spinning at the right speed or are the you know is it drawing the right power\N风扇转速是否正常，功耗是否正常，
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.03,0:02:51.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,is there something wrong with the node is the is the network flapping or is anything problem problem with the\N节点有没有问题，网络是不是在抖动，还是出了别的毛病，
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.34,0:02:56.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,network is the performance there right like there's all these sorts of checks and tests because GPUs are unreliable um\N网络性能是否达标。这类检查和测试五花八门，因为 GPU 并不可靠。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.87,0:03:02.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's all sorts of stuff around um the types of software you run on top of the GPU right many\N围绕 GPU 运行的软件类型也有各种讲究。很多人
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.56,0:03:07.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,people started off doing just bare metal right so when you go look at like hey Microsoft's first contracts\N人们一开始只是直接使用裸金属，所以你看微软的首批合同
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.01,0:03:13.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,with CoreWeave they were all bare metal right you just SSH in and Microsoft would set up their own stuff\N使用 CoreWeave 时，他们都是裸金属服务器，\N你只需通过 SSH 登录，微软会自行搭建他们的系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.56,0:03:20.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,but as we've stepped forward there's a lot more people want right people wanted Slurm installed okay that's simple people\N但当我们向前迈进时，大家想要的东西更多了：有人想装 Slurm，这很简单，还有人
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.06,0:03:26.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,wanted Kubernetes installed that's a little bit more difficult but still pretty simple people wanted Slurm on Kubernetes installed cuz\N想要安装Kubernetes，这稍微有点困难，但仍然相当简单，\N人们还想在Kubernetes上安装Slurm。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.53,0:03:30.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's easier to push out jobs and things like that right and now you're starting to see people do\N因为这样分发任务更方便。现在你开始看到人们需要
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.47,0:03:37.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,things like managed Ray services and all these things for RL and so there is a class of neoclouds\N像托管 Ray 服务这类东西，以及用于强化学习的各种服务，因此出现了一类新云厂商。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.44,0:03:40.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,that are building these things and there's a class of neoclouds that are like I don't care about that\N有些新云厂商在构建这些服务，而另一类新云厂商则说我不在乎这些，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.62,0:03:45.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm just going to build GPUs and rent them out at bare metal and and there is a difference in\N我就只做GPU，然后以裸金属的形式租出去，这中间是有区别的。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.65,0:03:51.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,cost right like the the clouds that have the good software also tend to charge more and and sort\N那些软件好的云服务商往往收费更高，这又回到了老模式，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.54,0:03:59.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,of returns back to the old school model where Google Microsoft Amazon had good software and they charged right and\N也就是谷歌、微软、亚马逊当年软件好、收费也高。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.26,0:04:04.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,so you know and and you see a lot of these cloud companies start trying to launch inference services\N所以你知道，你看到很多云公司开始尝试推出推理服务
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.48,0:04:12.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,and all these other things yeah So like that similarly in that vein I'll just get to the CPU ones\N还有其他这些事情，是的。类似地，我就直接讲CPU的部分了。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.14,0:04:16.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,where historically we have customers that ask for this with like open cloud that happened so that there's a\N历史上，我们的客户曾提出类似开放云的需求，因此出现了这种情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.78,0:04:21.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,bunch of people that are like oh I need my sandbox or CPU box running for a very very long\N一堆人说，我需要让我的沙盒或 CPU 服务器长时间运行
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.73,0:04:27.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,time can you give me like a $5 Hetzner type you know offering and I'm like well no because like\N你能给我一个像 Hetzner 那样五美元左右的套餐吗？我说，呃，不行，因为……
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.84,0:04:34.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,that is a bare metal machine that has no incurs very little cost but when you have something that's larger\N这是一台裸金属机器，几乎不产生成本，但当你处理更大规模的系统时，情况就不同了
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.23,0:04:38.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,software offering then there is more cost so it's hard to to compete with that so I would assume\N软件产品的话成本更高，因此很难与之竞争，所以我推测
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.23,0:04:42.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,also on the neoclouds that like the ones that are bare metal as you mentioned have a lower cost\N此外，像你提到的那些裸金属新云厂商，成本也更低。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.24,0:04:49.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,of sale than the the software ones um that moving just I was just curious about that like why the\N销售成本比软件类新云厂商更低。我只是好奇，为什么会出现这种情况，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.38,0:04:55.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,right to exist they had because it's sort of analogized with what we do but the real question is you\N它们有存在的理由，因为这有点像我们所做的事，但真正的问题是，你
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.61,0:05:00.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,brought this up which is directionally what we're thinking about is that CPUs are the new bottleneck like every\N提到了这一点，这正是我们目前思考的方向：CPU 正成为新的瓶颈。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.00,0:05:06.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,investor partner everyone that I talked to historically was just like GPU GPU GPU and now you had this big\N投资伙伴、我过去交谈过的每个人，都只关心 GPU、GPU、GPU，而现在你们出了这份
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.46,0:05:12.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,report about like CPUs and I'm like okay yes thank you and so you reported like this year will be\N关于CPU的报告，我说，好吧，谢谢，所以你报告说今年将会是
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.27,0:05:17.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,a bottleneck so just give us a high level TLDR why is CPU now bottleneck and what do you see?\N一个瓶颈，所以请简要说明一下，为什么现在CPU成了瓶颈，你看到了什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.37,0:05:25.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah I mean for the first few years of AI CPU was a real big lagger right sure you used it for some storage used it for some checkpointing\N是的，我的意思是，在 AI 发展的头几年，CPU 确实是个明显的短板，\N虽然你用它来做一些存储和检查点操作。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.55,0:05:29.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,used it for pre-processing your data and pre-training but it was pretty light and then\N做数据预处理和预训练，但负载很轻。后来
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.00,0:05:33.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,inference was also like the models just weren't good enough to be agentic you couldn't\N推理时也感觉模型还不够好，无法实现代理式行为，你无法让它做到。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.93,0:05:40.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know go step by step by step so there was no there was no capability for a model to go and do actions and string them together so then\N你知道，得一步一步来，所以当时模型还无法自主采取行动并把它们串联起来。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.68,0:05:46.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,it wasn't really it was like it was like you would send a string and it send a string back right simple inference and so there was not much need\N其实它就像你发送一段字符串，它就返回一段字符串，很简单地推理，因此并没有太多需求
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.79,0:05:56.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,for CPUs but then over the last few years or last couple years it's not even like last couple years right you know Q* and OpenAI had that and\N经历了那么多风波，但最终 o1 预览版上线了，我想大概是 15、16 个月前，感觉像是很久以前了。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.92,0:06:05.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,they had all that drama but then finally o1 preview launched I want to say like 15 16 months ago feels like much longer ago a long time ago Yeah\N他们之前闹了那么多风波，但最终o1预览版还是上线了，我想大概是15、\N16个月前的事了，感觉像是很久以前的事了，真的很久以前了。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.75,0:06:13.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,ages yeah but o1 was the first model sort of there and and we we sort of had a entire flood of models right like before people would do simple\N是的，但 o1 是首个出现的模型，之后我们迎来了大量模型的涌现，就像以前人们只会做简单的事情一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.91,0:06:19.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,things like check the output of the model with regex or something simple just to\N比如用正则表达式之类的简单方法检查模型的输出
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.41,0:06:23.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,see if it was doing structured properly doing structured outputs you know for function calling\N看看它有没有正确生成结构化输出，比如用于函数调用，
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.16,0:06:28.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,and things like this right but as we've stepped forward the the the checks on\N诸如此类。但随着我们往前走，对模型的检查
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.09,0:06:32.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,the model are much much larger integrated fully into training right with reinforcement learning right\N规模大得多，而且完全整合进训练，通过强化学习来实现。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.80,0:06:36.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,instead of just doing regex you're doing like various classifiers instead of doing classifiers you're\N不再只是正则匹配，而是各种分类器；不再只是分类器，
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.69,0:06:41.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,doing like code unit test and compilation instead of doing that you're running you know\N而是代码单元测试和编译；再往后，你运行的是
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.64,0:06:47.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,agentic flows where it's actually calling databases and stuff or you're interfacing with some environment\N代理式流程，比如它会真正调用数据库或其他操作，或者你正在与某个环境进行交互
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.49,0:06:52.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,that is heavy on CPU like a physics simulation or or biology simulation you just\N就像物理模拟或生物模拟那样对 CPU 负载很高的场景，你只需
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.50,0:06:57.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,kept stepping into more and more complicated things where the model outputs to checks it\N不断深入更复杂的事物，模型输出后进行检查
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.85,0:07:01.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,right this environment reinforcement learning environment and then goes back and trains on it and\N这个环境是强化学习环境，然后它会返回并在此环境中进行训练。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.72,0:07:05.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,and this loop has gotten tighter and tighter and tighter over the last couple years\N过去几年里，这个循环变得越来越紧密。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.29,0:07:10.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then more recently over the let's call it really the last 6 months you\N然后最近，大概过去六个月里，你
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.42,0:07:21.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,know code agent revenue has gone from a couple billion to north of 10 billion in like a very short amount of time and and these the horizon of these\N代码智能体的收入在极短时间内从几十亿美元涨到超过 100 亿美元，而这些智能体的任务时长
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.39,0:07:26.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,has also increased dramatically right like GPT-5.4 Codex can work for like 6-7 hours and\N也大幅增加。比如 GPT-5.4 Codex 能连续工作六七个小时，
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.44,0:07:33.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's like fine right and so you know it's it's in that time frame it's\N而且表现还不错。在这段时间里，它
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.33,0:07:40.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,doing all sorts of calls to databases it's doing calls to you know at least we we use a lot of cron servers but you know like whatever whatever it\N它在不断调用各种数据库，比如我们用了很多 cron 服务器，但不管怎样，不管它在做什么
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.48,0:07:44.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,is right there's anything and everything it can go ping check it out scrape\N就在那儿，它能做任何事，去 ping 一下看看，去抓取一下
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.42,0:07:48.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,and just work agentically on its own and that's also requiring a lot of CPUs\N并能自主地以智能体方式运行，这也需要大量 CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.48,0:07:52.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,so over the last 6 months that's ballooned as well in addition to the reinforcement\N因此，在过去六个月里，除了强化学习之外，这一数字也大幅增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.56,0:07:57.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,learning training loop getting tighter and tighter and so over the last 6 months we've\N训练循环越来越紧密，过去六个月里我们已经看到这一趋势不断加强。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.18,0:08:03.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,seen um the entire cloud market run out of CPUs right I don't know if\N我看到整个云市场CPU都快用完了，我不知道
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.42,0:08:07.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,you folks have interacted with GitHub a lot recently but it's really unstable I think\N不知道你们最近是不是经常用 GitHub，它真的很不稳定。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.56,0:08:11.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,you're the third person to mention that today Okay Yeah Yeah yeah so we've we've\N今天第三个人提到这个了。嗯，是的，没错，我们确实……
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.45,0:08:15.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,been we've been like checking GitHub's like stats on like how often is it down\N我们一直在查看 GitHub 的状态，比如它多久会宕机一次
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.30,0:08:19.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,how often does it fail to commit like you know whatever right it's it's terrible\N它经常无法提交，你知道的，反正就是太糟糕了
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.14,0:08:23.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,and that's because Microsoft sold all their CPUs that they had spare to other people\N这是因为微软把所有闲置的CPU都卖给了别人。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.08,0:08:28.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,right either internal use for their lab but you know not really more so like\N要么是内部实验室使用，但其实也就是那样了
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.36,0:08:33.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,external labs they signed deals with Anthropic and OpenAI and so they just have like\N外部实验室——他们和 Anthropic、OpenAI 签了协议，所以微软手里
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.10,0:08:42.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,no CPUs left right and we've seen you know the same at many other firms right so whereas before you'd have like you know have many GPU servers per CPU\NCPU 已经用完了，我们也在其他很多公司看到过这种情况，\N所以以前你可能每台 CPU 配多台 GPU 服务器，但现在不行了。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.85,0:08:50.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,server and so you'd be like you know 100 megawatts of GPUs would be served by even like 1 megawatt or less of CPUs nowadays the ratio is like getting\N正在大幅缩小，无论强化学习训练还是代理式推理都是如此。所以
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.98,0:08:56.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,much much closer both for RL training and and for inference agentic inference so then\N在强化学习训练和代理式推理方面都更加接近了，所以接下来
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.80,0:09:03.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,you you've just seen everyone run out of CPUs Amazon's volumes on CPUs of CPU\N你看到所有人都把 CPU 用光了。亚马逊的 CPU 服务器
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.19,0:09:07.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,servers they're installing have 3x year on year right from this year versus last year\N安装量同比增长了三倍，今年对比去年。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.76,0:09:13.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,and so that there's just no capacity anywhere and that's causing a lot of instability\N因此，任何地方都没有产能，这导致了很大的不稳定性。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.28,0:09:17.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,not just in GitHub but probably other places too I mean a lot of infrastructure\N不仅在 GitHub 上，可能在其他地方也是如此，我的意思是，很多基础设施都是如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.76,0:09:21.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,today we talked about this like every day it's normal to see that some infra\N今天我们就这个问题聊了聊，就像每天一样，看到一些基础设施问题再正常不过了。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.46,0:09:29.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,provider be it GitHub or being like an actual not to name like they go down like it's become quite a constant thing and so could be lack of CPUs\N提供商宕机，不管是 GitHub 还是别的什么，已经成了常态。这可能是 CPU 不足，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.79,0:09:33.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,but also scale of the workloads and what not so that everyone's infra code is\N也可能是工作负载规模太大等等。所以现在每个人的基础设施代码都是
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.95,0:09:37.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,vibe coded Yeah it could be that everyone's infra code is vibe coded yeah could\N氛围编码出来的。是的，也可能每个人的基础设施代码都是氛围编码的，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.52,0:09:45.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,that be as well I don't think it's all but there could be there could be parts of that that is there and so what I see which is interesting\N这也有可能。我不认为全是这样，但可能有一部分是。我觉得有意思的是，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.24,0:09:53.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,as well as the number of CPU workloads or the number of that are running on us so Daytona has basically three use cases so it's like code and command\N运行在我们这里的 CPU 工作负载数量。Daytona 基本上有三类用例：代码与命令
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.30,0:10:02.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,execution so if you like a a Claude Code type of thing needs to run on a We have computer use cases which we see actually growing really fast.\N执行，比如 Claude Code 这类东西需要在 CPU 上运行；\N还有电脑操作场景，我们看到它增长得非常快。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.39,0:10:06.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've now launched today we announced our Windows sandbox which runs on a CPU.\N今天我们正式发布：基于 CPU 运行的 Windows 沙箱。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.41,0:10:12.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you need an agent to do like on legacy software which is like all finance, all support, all um that's all there.\N所以如果你需要一个智能体来处理像旧软件这样的任务，比如所有财务、所有支持，这些都在里面。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.75,0:10:18.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I'll also to your point like reinforcement learning, we have a bunch of people that usually use like Kubernetes.\N但就你提到的强化学习而言，我们有很多客户通常用 Kubernetes，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.26,0:10:19.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now they would use us.\N现在他们会用我们。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.32,0:10:25.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the interesting thing is the the size and scale of these loads are insanely large and they're growing insanely large.\N但有趣的是，这些负载的规模和体量大得惊人，而且还在急剧扩大。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.10,0:10:28.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're like the smallest cloud in the world.\N而我们大概是世界上最小的云。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.80,0:10:36.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,So my interest to what in the question is like if we as a very very small company have this much, what does that do at the large scale, right?\N所以，我对这个问题的兴趣在于，如果我们作为一家非常非常小的公司，\N已经能做到这种程度，那么在大规模上会怎样呢，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.29,0:10:39.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like so um and we've had I'm curious if you have any insight on this,\N就像这样，呃，我很好奇，你对这个问题有什么见解吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.90,0:10:45.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,but just just RL let alone the long running agents which are on their own, we we see customers coming in.\N但仅仅是强化学习，更不用说那些独立运行的长期智能体，我们已经看到客户纷纷上门。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.47,0:10:49.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,One of them ran a million one single customer yesterday in the span of 6 hours.\N其中一位客户昨天在 6 小时内跑了一百万个这样的 CPU 工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.40,0:10:50.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like 1 million of these CPU workloads.\N像一百万个这样的CPU工作负载。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.02,0:10:52.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's one customer.\N这就是一位客户。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.10,0:10:53.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so like how many of these customers are doing RL?\N那么，有多少客户在使用强化学习呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.71,0:10:54.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're going to need this.\N他们将会需要这个。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.69,0:10:57.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I don't know if you have any insights on this, but I'm just curious.\N我不确定你有没有什么见解，只是有点好奇。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.56,0:11:01.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I mean I mean there there there there are some pretty uh shocking metrics.\N呃，我的意思是，有些数据确实相当惊人。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.79,0:11:04.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like a million vCPUs sounds insane.\N一百万个 vCPU 听起来太疯狂了。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.36,0:11:12.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but there some of the some of the scale of the workloads and contracts people are signing are are even like more ridiculous than that, right?\N但有些工作负载和合同的规模，人们签下的甚至比那还荒谬，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.08,0:11:13.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I'm sure that's because we're really small.\N嗯，我猜是因为我们实在太小了。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.76,0:11:14.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's what I Yeah, yeah.\N我就是这个意思。对，对。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.84,0:11:19.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So so I guess I guess like when you look at like again like when you look at like the Anthropic and OpenAI of the world,\N所以当你看 Anthropic 和 OpenAI 这样的公司，
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.76,0:11:24.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,they have they have fully just eaten the entire capacity of multiple clouds, right?\N他们已经把多个云平台的全部算力都吃干抹净了，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.26,0:11:29.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,A lot of the impetus for the recent Amazon and OpenAI deal was yes, OpenAI wanted money, yes,\N最近亚马逊与OpenAI达成交易的很大动因是，没错，OpenAI确实需要资金，没错，
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.92,0:11:34.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,they needed compute, but they also just like went to Amazon and were like give us your CPU.\N他们需要计算能力，于是直接找到亚马逊，说给我们你的CPU就行。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.08,0:11:35.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,CPUs, yeah.\NCPU，没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.38,0:11:36.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.13,0:11:43.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and and before OpenAI's stack was pretty much only on x86 CPUs, but Amazon had tons of Arm CPUs and so they ported the whole thing, right?\N嗯，之前 OpenAI 的系统基本只运行在 x86 CPU 上，\N但亚马逊有大量 Arm CPU，所以他们就把整个系统都移植过去了，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.90,0:11:47.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like anywhere I'll I'll port my code base to get uh access, right?\N就像只要能拿到 CPU，我在哪儿都愿意把代码库移植过去，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.70,0:11:48.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,To access to CPUs.\N访问 CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.63,0:11:53.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so this is like the the level of like and it's not that difficult to port port from x86 to Arm, but you know,\N所以这就像是那种程度，从 x86 迁移到 Arm 并不难，你懂的。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.65,0:11:56.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,like there's there's very few dependencies that aren't working now,\N现在几乎没有不工作的依赖项了。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.61,0:12:02.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,but um this is the level of like um engineering people are willing to go to, right?\N但呃，这就是工程师们愿意做到的程度，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.27,0:12:09.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cuz usually devs are too lazy to do anything um and they'll just go get capacity elsewhere, but there isn't capacity anywhere else.\N因为通常开发者都懒得动手，只会去别处找算力，但别处根本没算力。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.16,0:12:11.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so I mean that's interesting like we're all x86.\N是的，这挺有意思的，我们大家都是 x86。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.23,0:12:12.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's all we have.\N我们只有这些。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.18,0:12:14.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We don't have our our ARM at the moment.\N我们目前没有自己的 Arm。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.08,0:12:20.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,But then like there's those two which I know, but also like NVIDIA has their like CPU, other people building out their CPUs.\N但除了那两个我了解的，英伟达也有自己的CPU，其他人也在开发自己的CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.41,0:12:22.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's also differences between these CPUs.\N这些 CPU 之间也存在差异。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.48,0:12:24.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are there just going to be like these general purpose CPUs?\N难道以后就只有这些通用型 CPU 了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.28,0:12:26.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's also like you probably know more about this than I do.\N你可能比我更了解这方面的情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.59,0:12:28.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm just like super curious.\N我就是特别好奇。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.68,0:12:30.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um on the types of CPUs?\N嗯，关于 CPU 的类型？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.21,0:12:32.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like now there's so many there used to be just like x86 and ARM.\N现在种类这么多，以前基本上只有 x86 和 Arm。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.90,0:12:34.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,That was it like for the most part.\N基本上就是这样了。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.48,0:12:36.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now there's different types of CPUs.\N现在有不同类型的CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.16,0:12:40.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is it just because everyone's run out or are they like better at some things than others?\N是因为大家都用尽了，还是说他们在某些方面确实更擅长？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.64,0:12:49.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are there anything I mean usually what happens like when there's a gold rush is the person with a broken pickaxe can also sell their pickaxes.\N通常来说，就像淘金热时期，即使拿着一把坏镐的人也能把镐卖出去。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.91,0:12:50.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah.\N对，对。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.90,0:12:55.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but like yeah, I mean this the CPU market is like quite dynamic, right?\N嗯，不过说实话，CPU市场确实相当活跃，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.88,0:12:57.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you know, it it was mostly Intel AMD.\N嗯，你知道的，主要是英特尔和 AMD。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.24,0:13:00.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,I assume you mostly use Intel and AMD CPUs.\N我猜你主要用的是英特尔和 AMD 的 CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.16,0:13:03.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um Both of them have said they're like fully sold out.\N两者都表示已经完全售罄。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.68,0:13:06.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,They've sent price increase notices to their customers.\N他们已向客户发出涨价通知。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.75,0:13:08.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so they're not even competing with each other anymore.\N所以他们现在甚至都不再互相竞争了。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.41,0:13:11.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're just like how many can I make and sell?\N他们只是在想我能生产多少并卖出去多少？
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.21,0:13:14.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and likewise like Amazon had their Graviton CPUs.\N而且就像亚马逊有他们的自研 Graviton CPU 一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.49,0:13:15.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,They've had what?\N他们出到第几代了？
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.32,0:13:17.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Five, six generations now.\N到现在已经五六代了。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.68,0:13:20.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um And NVIDIA has their Vera CPU.\N嗯，英伟达有他们的 Vera CPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.28,0:13:20.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.72,0:13:23.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And NVIDIA has their Grace and Vera CPUs.\N英伟达拥有其 Grace 和 Vera 处理器。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.40,0:13:26.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and no one really deployed Grace standalone CPU boxes.\N而且没人真正部署过独立的 Grace CPU 服务器。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.86,0:13:30.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,There was like a couple small deployments that NVIDIA NVIDIA did for PR with people,\N英伟达为了公关效果，和几家客户做过几个小规模部署，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.93,0:13:34.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,but in reality there's like very few like standalone CPU deployments that NVIDIA was able to do.\N但实际上，英伟达能够实现的独立CPU部署非常少。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.03,0:13:35.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.42,0:13:38.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but now well, just they're just not as good, right?\N嗯，但现在他们确实没那么好了，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.16,0:13:38.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.39,0:13:41.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but now as we step forward, maybe their CPU got better.\N但如今我们向前迈进，也许他们的CPU变得更强大了。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.56,0:13:44.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um maybe they're bundling better, but also just because they have capacity.\N也许他们捆绑得更好了，但也确实是因为他们有产能。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.72,0:13:45.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because no one else has them.\N因为别人都没有。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.75,0:13:52.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, they're they're they're able to get a lot more contracts on their uh Vera CPUs uh that are going to deploy sort of later this year,\N是的，他们现在能拿到更多关于Vera CPU的合同，这些CPU预计将在今年稍晚时候部署。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.56,0:13:55.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,early next year time frame um is when they start deploying.\N明年年初左右，他们就会开始部署。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.40,0:13:57.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's sort of like a very um dynamic market.\N所以这有点像一个非常动态的市场。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.92,0:14:03.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then and then you've got like Microsoft and Google are starting to deploy their CPUs in volumes.\N然后，微软和谷歌也开始大规模部署他们的CPU了。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.06,0:14:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um ARM is going to launch a CPU in like a few weeks uh that Meta is going to adopt and a few others are going to adopt um like Cloudflare.\N嗯，Arm 几周后将推出一款 CPU，Meta 将采用，\N还有像 Cloudflare 这样的公司也会采用。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.44,0:14:15.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so there's going to be a lot more proliferation like Arm standalone rather than like Arm licensing the IP to someone.\N因此会出现更多 Arm 独立芯片，而不是 Arm 把 IP 授权给别人。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.55,0:14:22.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,So there's a lot more um diversification in the market um which which happens when there's a gold rush, right?\N所以市场上有更多的多样化，这在出现淘金热时就会发生，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.55,0:14:29.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we'll see what actually is the best quality and is left standing as the sort of supply demand gap get closes.\N随后我们将看到，当供需差距逐渐缩小后，究竟哪种质量的产品能够脱颖而出，保持领先。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.76,0:14:30.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.20,0:14:36.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,But it seems that supply and demand will still grow like at least what I see like one the RL and it it seems like RL is mostly done,\N但看起来供需仍会继续增长。至少从我看到的情况，强化学习大多是在后训练阶段完成，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.40,0:14:44.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, they do post trading on RL, but we have now vendors and companies that are pitching and creating services that do RL in real time.\N你知道，他们确实会用强化学习做后训练，但现在已有供应商在提供实时强化学习服务。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.86,0:14:50.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And since you have like some agents you have some SaaS that's an agentic in the background and then\N而且因为你们有一些智能体，有些 SaaS 在后台以代理式方式运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.72,0:14:56.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,it will do RL at the end of the day basically to like learn against what it has done.\N说到底，它最终会进行强化学习，以根据自身行为进行学习。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.21,0:14:57.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that grows.\N于是它不断增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.37,0:15:05.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,But also these long running agents, if they the way it seems to be working directionally is if the agents can work longer and solve for more things,\N但还有这些长时间运行的智能体，从目前看来，它们若能持续工作更久，解决更多问题，效果会更好。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.58,0:15:11.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,you can essentially ask them to do more and they will spin up more and more of these agents which means more and more CPU boxes.\N你基本上可以要求它们做更多事情，它们就会不断启动更多的智能体，这意味着需要更多的 CPU 服务器。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.66,0:15:18.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,So do you see that like from your purview do you like I understand market dynamics and that'll probably converge at some point,\N所以从你的角度看，我理解市场动态，它们最终可能会趋于一致。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.45,0:15:22.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,but I feel it's getting wider before it's shrinking the need for that.\N但我感觉在需求减少之前，差距反而在扩大。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.44,0:15:28.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I mean it it it's that's totally the case because initially all the RL was like, let's do math proofs.\N是的，我的意思是，这完全符合实际情况，因为最初所有的强化学习都是围绕数学证明展开的。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.28,0:15:31.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I was like, okay, math proofs are really low on resources.\N我当时心想，数学证明所需的资源实在太少了。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.35,0:15:33.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And also the model, right?\N还有这个模型，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.12,0:15:37.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,The generator will generate tons of output and then it'll send the correct answer or what\N生成器会产生大量输出，然后把正确答案，或者
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.87,0:15:41.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,it thinks is the correct answer to the server and then the server will verify it.\N它认为正确的答案发给服务器，然后由服务器验证。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.79,0:15:44.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but as we've moved forward, right?\N但随着我们不断前进，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.18,0:15:45.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like it's it's not just that.\N不只是这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.44,0:15:46.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like,\N就像是，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.27,0:15:50.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,oh actually the model is committing many times or it's like trying to\N哦，实际上模型在反复提交代码，或者是在尝试
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.55,0:15:53.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,compile many times or it's trying to do unit tests throughout its agentic process.\N频繁编译，或者它在代理式流程中不断尝试单元测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.98,0:16:00.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, now that's that's increasing the frequency in which the generator, i.e. the model, is sending to the verifier.\N现在，这相当于提高了生成器，也就是模型，向验证器发送的频率。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.30,0:16:02.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and that loop gets tighter and tighter and tighter.\N而且这个循环变得越来越紧密。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.94,0:16:10.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,And as we as we continue to move to more complex RL, it's like the model will actually uh be verifying its output constantly, right?\N随着我们不断迈向更复杂的强化学习，模型实际上会持续验证其输出，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.50,0:16:14.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like if you imagine um let's say models that are training over the next year or two is\N就像你想象一下，假设未来一两年内模型正在训练
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.98,0:16:19.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,is let's say a robot model that's verifying and that's that's in in a like a world model,\N比如一个正在验证的机器人模型，它处于类似世界模型的环境中。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.49,0:16:20.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.05,0:16:24.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So uh VLM is is navigating across the world trying to pick up things, put them down.\N嗯，VLM 在虚拟世界里移动，试图捡起东西、放下东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.84,0:16:29.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every single action needs to be verified against the physics model that is sitting on some CPUs.\N每一项操作都必须与运行在某些 CPU 上的物理模型进行核对。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.68,0:16:38.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that's that's insanely way more CPUs than you need for say doing unit tests or running a math proof, right?\N所以，这比做单元测试或运行数学证明所需的 CPU 多出太多了，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.05,0:16:41.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when we look at like o1, that's like all it could do was math, right?\N当我们看 o1 的时候，它能做的就只有数学运算，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.07,0:16:48.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and as we look at like you know, sort of uh GPT-5.4 or Opus 4.6, like it's okay agentic software,\N嗯，像 GPT-5.4 或 Opus 4.6，它们作为代理式软件已经算可以了，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.86,0:16:52.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,but like as we move forward to the next stage of, you know, whatever's coming,\N但随着我们迈向下一个阶段，也就是接下来可能出现的任何事物，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.73,0:16:58.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's going to be models that can understand, oh, I need to tie my shoe and like when I tie it,\N它会理解：哦，我需要系鞋带，而系的时候要用多大力量，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.44,0:17:00.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,what's the strength strength, yeah. like what's the tensile strength?\N强度是多少？比如抗拉强度？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.90,0:17:06.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,All these things like as to the the has to be calculated cuz the verifier is just generating, you know, what's the next step.\N所有这些都必须被计算，因为验证器只是在生成下一步该做什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.26,0:17:13.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but every step needs to be checked way more often and the intensity of that calculation for checking the step it goes up a time.\N但每一步都需要更频繁地检查，而检查这一步的计算强度也会随之增加。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.08,0:17:13.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.40,0:17:19.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,But there's also another thing and you probably know better than I is like the the the level\N但还有另一件事，你可能比我更清楚，就是那个程度
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.37,0:17:26.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,of the the the strength of the GPUs can handle in parallel a certain amount of CPUs boxes.\NGPU 的算力可以并行处理多少台 CPU 服务器。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.06,0:17:29.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so as we get next generations of GPUs,\N因此，当我们迎来下一代 GPU 时，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.15,0:17:38.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,I feel that they will be able to spin up manage or work on more CPUs than they do now which is another stressor on CPUs now.\N我觉得他们将能够启动、管理或处理比现在更多的 CPU，这也会给 CPU 带来新的压力。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.88,0:17:40.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I mean that's that's certainly the case, right?\N是的，那确实如此，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.79,0:17:44.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,GPU Well, GPUs are also just like getting way higher power, right?\NGPU，其实 GPU 的功耗也在大幅上升，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.44,0:17:49.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So one GPU will equal many many more CPUs over time, right?\N所以随着时间推移，一块GPU将相当于众多CPU，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.12,0:17:55.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and GPUs are getting more expensive gen on gen on gen, whereas vCPUs are flat, slightly down.\N而且 GPU 一代比一代贵，而 vCPU 的价格持平甚至略有下降。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.22,0:17:55.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.73,0:17:58.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and so certainly it's a different scale, right?\N嗯，所以这确实是一个不同的规模，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.80,0:18:02.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like one Blackwell versus one Rubin, performance is up X.\N一块 Blackwell 对比一块 Rubin，性能提升了 X 倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.64,0:18:04.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Price is also up X.\N价格也上涨了 X。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.12,0:18:12.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um whereas, you know, you may buy last generation CPU, new generation CPU and there's 192 vCPUs in this gen and last gen was like 96, right?\N嗯，比如说，你可能买上一代的CPU，或者新一代的CPU，\N这一代有192个vCPU，上一代大概是96个，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.97,0:18:18.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So now you've got way more CPUs, but the the price increase is equivalent to what you got in additional vCPUs.\N现在你的CPU数量多了很多，但价格涨幅相当于你获得的额外vCPU所带来的成本增加。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.76,0:18:23.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's like sort of yeah, the the ratio will grow in the favor of vCPUs,\N所以比例会向 vCPU 倾斜，
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.25,0:18:28.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,but the cost will be sort of also probably in the direction of CPUs, but not sure how much.\N但成本可能也会向 CPU 方向上升，不过不确定会升多少。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.85,0:18:29.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.19,0:18:35.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and also the other stressor on that and we've seen this with with larger customers when they have\N而且另一个压力源也存在，我们之前在大客户身上就看到过这种情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.61,0:18:40.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,like they don't they have like a time allotment for GPUs and they don't want their GPUs to be idle.\N他们好像有分配给 GPU 的时间配额，不希望 GPU 处于空闲状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.40,0:18:48.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,So they rather pay uh for warm pool running CPUs so that whenever tasks come from the GPU, the CPUs are they're hot.\N所以他们宁愿为持续运行的热池CPU付费，这样当GPU有任务过来时，CPU就已经处于就绪状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.74,0:18:50.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're essentially working, right?\NCPU 实际上已经在工作了，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.52,0:18:54.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So they'll we we I say we cuz we do mostly CPUs are certainly the cheap resource.\N所以我们会说，因为我们主要做 CPU，这显然是成本较低的资源。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.92,0:18:57.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't know if we're cheap, but cheap resource for this.\N我不知道我们是不是便宜，但这个资源确实很便宜。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.26,0:19:04.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that spends more GPUs actually just because the cost of having an idle GPU is to is way more expensive, right?\N所以实际上会用更多GPU，因为让GPU闲置的成本要高得多，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.04,0:19:06.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's actually like a really interesting point, right?\N是的，这实际上是个非常有趣的观点，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.97,0:19:10.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,The business model is like no one does I mean sure, there's on demand GPUs,\N这个商业模式——我是说，确实有按需 GPU，
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.97,0:19:16.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,but like Lambda has like 50,000 plus GPUs and only 4,000 of them are on demand, right?\N但就像 Lambda 有超过 5 万块 GPU，其中只有 4000 块是按需可用的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.67,0:19:17.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,And they're always sold out.\N而且总是卖光。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.84,0:19:20.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,So like no one really has on demand GPUs.\N所以其实没人真的拥有按需 GPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.10,0:19:27.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everyone's signing at minimum like long-term, you know, multi-month contracts, but in most cases multi-year contracts.\N大家都在签至少长期的合同，你知道的，几个月起步，大多数是多年期的合同。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.58,0:19:32.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and so like CPUs have been used to like you can spin them up and down, right?\N嗯，就像 CPU 可以随时启动和关闭一样，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.39,0:19:34.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's why everyone moved to the cloud, right?\N这就是为什么大家都转向了云端，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.96,0:19:42.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but with these RL workloads, it's like, okay, the GPU: the generator, the model running on a GPU generated a bunch of stuff.\N但这些强化学习工作负载的情况是，好吧，GPU作为生成器，运行在GPU上的模型生成了一大堆内容。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.09,0:19:44.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,It sends it to the verifier.\N它将其发送给验证器。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.08,0:19:46.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,If the verifier is not ready and waiting Then it's idle.\N如果验证器没有提前准备好并等待，GPU 就会空闲。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.17,0:19:46.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then it's waiting.\N然后它在等待。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.76,0:19:46.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.95,0:19:47.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like the GPU is just sitting there.\N就像 GPU 就那样闲置着。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.97,0:19:51.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's like, okay, well, I've already paid for this.\N反正我已经付过钱了，就这样吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.21,0:19:51.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.72,0:20:00.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you can't get your instantaneous you know you know resources spun up on the CPU side and in fact you should do it preemptively so it's not\N所以如果你无法立即获得资源，你知道的，就在CPU端预先启动起来，\N事实上你应该提前做好准备，这样就不会耽误了
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.28,0:20:05.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,like loading you know the the simulator that you or the generation the environment\N就像加载你所知道的模拟器，或是生成的环境
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.32,0:20:08.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,right you you're wasting money so yeah like that that makes a lot of sense.\N没错，你这是在浪费钱，所以这确实很有道理。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.09,0:20:11.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And not only that then you have that running and then as soon as those are running you're\N这些一跑起来，你又去启动另一个热池，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.24,0:20:16.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,spinning up another warm pool of these so that every new iteration of them are are continually growing.\N启动另一个热池，使它们的每一次迭代都能持续增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.49,0:20:18.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what does that mean generally?\N那通常意味着什么呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.40,0:20:26.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we skipped over RAM we didn't talk about that where it's like GPU was a bottleneck RAM was a bottleneck and now CPUs.\N所以我们跳过了内存，没提它，因为之前是GPU成为瓶颈，后来是内存成为瓶颈，现在轮到CPU了。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.09,0:20:32.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,So just very closer to home for most people is that like it's very hard to buy a PC today because it's like super expensive is is that\N对大多数人来说，更贴近生活的是，现在买台电脑非常困难，因为实在太贵了。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.63,0:20:36.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,happening to the CPUs because we just mentioned that they're like they're fairly inexpensive\N这种情况会发生在 CPU 上吗？因为我们刚才提到它们相当便宜，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.53,0:20:41.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,and flat does the market pressure now demand sort of that these prices now increase?\N而如今市场压力是否要求这些价格现在上涨呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.00,0:20:47.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah I mean it's it's pretty much the case for all like PCs laptops building a PC\N是的，其实对所有电脑、笔记本电脑来说都是这样，组装一台电脑
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.04,0:20:54.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,that it's hard to get you know Apple is pretty sold out of like Mac minis for example.\N要知道，苹果的Mac mini之类的机型基本上已经售罄了。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.96,0:20:59.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we bought a bunch of Mac minis because people are switching from you know people who\N我们买了不少 Mac mini，因为很多人正在从其他设备转过来。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.09,0:21:02.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,used a bunch of Excel and like Windows are like okay I want to use Claude Code and\N用了一堆 Excel，还有 Windows，就是想试试 Claude Code
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.45,0:21:08.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,OS X is obviously a better um dev environment right so we just bought a bunch of Mac\N显然，macOS 是一个更好的开发环境，所以我们买了一堆 Mac。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.89,0:21:13.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,minis and people are deploying them and using them and and sort of I think similar has happened\NMac mini，人们正在部署和使用它们。我觉得情况类似，
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.85,0:21:19.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,across the space and then data centers are way more of an inelastic buyer of resources and\N在这一领域中，数据中心对资源的采购则更加缺乏弹性。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.18,0:21:24.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,so that's also caused prices to go up right so like GPUs always were expensive and video's margins\N这也推高了价格。GPU 一直很贵，英伟达的利润率
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.71,0:21:29.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,have always been you know 70% plus CPUs the margins were not that high but they're creeping up\N一直高达 70% 以上；CPU 的利润率没那么高，但正在上升，
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.69,0:21:35.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,because Intel and AMD are raising prices and they're tight memory has like 4x in price over the\N因为英特尔和 AMD 在涨价，而且供应紧张。内存价格过去一年涨了约 4 倍，
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.80,0:21:40.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,last like year and it's going to continue to go up and then now storage SSD right\N还会继续涨；现在轮到存储，SSD
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.82,0:21:45.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,so it's like all of the resources are SSDs are also up like three four x in price\N所以所有资源都在涨，SSD 也涨了三四倍，
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.77,0:21:49.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,and going to keep going up at least another like 60% not as much as DRAM but up\N而且还会继续上涨，至少再涨60%左右，虽然没有DRAM涨得那么多，但涨幅也不小。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.60,0:21:56.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,a lot and so between these like four like these things right it's like well the CPU capacity\N很多。在这四类东西之间——CPU、
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.31,0:22:03.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,for Intel and AMD is somewhat fungible between and substrate and all these things somewhat fungible between PCs\N英特尔和 AMD 的产能，在 PC 和数据中心之间、在基板等环节上，某种程度上可以互换；
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.31,0:22:09.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,and and data centers RAM and storage are very fungible and so you've ended up with this like\N内存和存储则高度可互换。于是你陷入了这样一个
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.18,0:22:15.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,conundrum that like look screw the screw the like normally humans screw the humans yeah you have to\N怪圈：算了，反正吃亏的总是普通人。你得
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.32,0:22:21.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,buy a Mac Mac mini now otherwise you'll never escape the permanent underclass is like the thought process.\N现在就买一台 Mac mini，否则永远逃不出底层——大概就是这个思路。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.52,0:22:29.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And one last note before we're close to the end but one thing not financial advice like Intel was in a very bad spot like quite like recently.\N最后再补充一点，虽然我们快结束了，但要说明一下，这并非财务建议，就像英特尔最近处境非常糟糕一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.05,0:22:29.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Still are.\N仍然如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.76,0:22:32.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah but does this pull them out?\N但这样能把它拉出困境吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.34,0:22:40.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I mean they'll do better but like it's not like it's like a long-term like you know oh the company's saved right?\N嗯，我是说他们表现会更好，但并不是说公司就真的长期得救了，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.60,0:22:46.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Company's valued on like future cash flows but like and also like some potentiality they get like\N公司估值基于未来的现金流，但也基于其潜在可能性。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.71,0:22:49.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Apple or someone else as a customer and this is actually like the funnier thing is it's\N苹果或其他客户。更有趣的是，
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.96,0:22:54.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,not because CPU demand is so high Intel have some short-term profits from that but you know\N不是因为CPU需求太高，英特尔因此获得了一些短期利润，但你知道
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.07,0:22:58.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,others will catch up AMD and Amazon and others will catch up on capacity that they have.\N其他公司也会赶上，比如 AMD 和亚马逊，它们在产能上会追上来。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.22,0:23:05.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,More importantly is that AI is buying all the capacity on 3 nanometer and 2 nanometer in a couple\N更重要的是，AI 正在短时间内买下了所有 3 纳米和 2 纳米的产能。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.82,0:23:09.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,years that you know people are having to turn to other directions right like one of the like you\N这些年，你知道人们不得不转向其他方向，比如其中一个，就像你所说的那样
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.70,0:23:15.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,know people make all these like nonsense reasons up why NVIDIA acquired Groq part of it was because they\N人们总是编出各种荒谬的理由来解释英伟达收购Groq的原因，其中一部分原因确实是因为他们
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.96,0:23:22.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,want to have really fast inference but like part of it is that Groq is manufactured on Samsung right?\N我想实现非常快速的推理，但其中一部分原因是 Groq 是在三星制造的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.68,0:23:27.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because there's no 3 nanometer capacity for them at TSMC they need a chip somewhere else and\N由于台积电没有3纳米产能，他们不得不在其他地方寻找芯片代工。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.12,0:23:30.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you just if AI is as crazy as like we believe it is and demand is\N如果 AI 真像我们想的那么疯狂，需求也
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.76,0:23:33.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,as crazy as we believe it is it's going to be even crazier next year and so\N真像我们想的那么疯狂，那明年还会更疯狂。所以
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.61,0:23:37.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,like just make any decent chip and it'll sell right is like sort of the philosophy there.\N只要做出一块像样的芯片，就一定能卖出去，大概就是这种理念。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.94,0:23:42.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Obviously there's a lot more they're doing there on the architecture and stuff but same applies to like Apple is\N显然，他们在架构等方面还做了很多事，但苹果的情况也是一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.63,0:23:49.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,getting squeezed out right like TSMC told them hey like get off of 3 nanometer move to 2 nanometer faster right?\N被挤得喘不过气。就像台积电告诉他们：离开 3 纳米，加快转到 2 纳米，
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.88,0:23:54.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because all the AI chips are on 3 nanometer and it takes time right small mobile chips are\N因为所有 AI 芯片都在 3 纳米上，而这需要时间。小型移动芯片
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.19,0:24:00.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,easier to make than big AI chips so all the AI chips are moving to 3 nanometer now right?\N制造起来比大芯片更容易，所以现在所有的AI芯片都在转向3纳米，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.46,0:24:06.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,MI350 from late last year from AMD or Trainium 3 and TPU v7 from late last year or\N去年底发布的 AMD MI350 或 Trainium 3，以及去年底发布的 TPU v7
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.94,0:24:15.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,slash early this year from Amazon and Google or you know NVIDIA is launching Rubin next week right?\N今年早些时候亚马逊和谷歌的产品，或者英伟达下周要发布的 Rubin，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.41,0:24:21.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's that's also so all these things are 3 nanometer and and they're just telling Apple to get off.\N这些也都是 3 纳米，而台积电只是在让苹果让出产能。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:21.48,0:24:25.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're telling Qualcomm and MediaTek to get off and all three of these companies are like oh maybe we\N他们也让高通和联发科让出产能，这三家公司都在想：也许我们
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.96,0:24:31.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,should use Intel because they're not telling us to get off because they don't they can't manufacture AI chips.\N该用英特尔，因为英特尔没有要求他们让出产能，因为英特尔造不了 AI 芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.80,0:24:35.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah so so it's it's pretty it's pretty tough for everyone.\N是啊，对每个人来说都挺难的。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.16,0:24:41.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I have like a bunch of questions I'd love to ask you we're like we have 20 seconds left so the next question I ask\N呃，我有一堆问题想问你，我们只剩20秒了，那我下一个问题就是
Dialogue: 0,0:24:41.52,0:24:48.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,you is probably going to go off so with that I'll just like keep us on time and appreciate so much for coming and talking to us.\N可能就收不住了。所以我就先控制一下时间，非常感谢你来交流。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:48.76,0:24:51.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much.\N非常感谢你。
